<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Joanna la Beltraneja</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1462–1530</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Joanna la Beltraneja was the daughter of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-iv-of-castile">Henry IV of Castile</a>, whose enemies claimed she was the child of the courtier Beltrán de la Cueva. Backed by her uncle Afonso V of Portugal, she contested the throne with Isabella I in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-castilian-succession">War of the Castilian Succession</a> of 1475–1479. After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-alcacovas">Treaty of Alcáçovas</a> she lived in Portugal until her death.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/joanna-la-beltraneja.jpg" alt="Joanna la Beltraneja" width="320" height="237" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: António de Holanda · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Joana,_a_Excelente_Senhora_-_The_Portuguese_Genealogy_(Genealogia_dos_Reis_de_Portugal).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
